{% comment %}
  Photo Upload - product page entry point
  Version: 2026-09-12.1

  The single line a product template needs:

      {% render 'photo-upload', product: product %}

  Add it to both product templates. Everything below is shared, so a change to
  any snippet reaches both without re-pasting.

  IMPORTANT: {% render %} has an isolated scope - unlike the deprecated
  {% include %}, it does NOT inherit the parent's variables. `product` must be
  passed in above and threaded down to each variant below. Omit it and the
  metafield guards quietly evaluate false, rendering nothing at all, with no
  error to tell you why.

  The four variant snippets are self-selecting: each opens with
  {% if product.metafields.custom.image_uploader_shape == '<shape>' %}, so
  exactly one produces output. No conditional is needed here.

  Not included, because they belong on other templates:
    cart-quantity-control  -> cart template, above the cart items
    photo-upload-replacement -> the replacement page template
{% endcomment %}
{% render 'photo-upload-styles' %}
{% render 'photo-upload-core' %}
{% render 'photo-upload-square', product: product %}
{% render 'photo-upload-rectangle', product: product %}
{% render 'photo-upload-bulk-square', product: product %}
{% render 'photo-upload-bulk-rectangle', product: product %}
{% render 'cart-button-control' %}
